{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences","id":838068,"title":"Hunter versus Mortal games - Differences?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T08:46:23-08:00","id":838068,"title":"Hunter versus Mortal games - Differences?","content":"On another thread, I discussed how I felt about the core mortal game &quot;eatting&quot; a lot of Hunter stuff. Professional Training, Cult-like merits, Horrors. To me, that was always what mortal games were about, and HtV simply took all that to the next level. The major advantage of a HtV game was that it actually focused on mortals as a real power in their own right. Thus, Risking Willpower and all the organizations in the know. Mortals are dangerous when they unite, and thus Tactics. Some really great ideas here. Meanwhile, after the core book? There's really not a lot of mortal-specific stuff that comes out. Sure, there was the generic Second Sight and Reliquary books, but those were self contained mini-games, not for core mortal stuff. Same with Inferno, Immortals. And the Armory books and Book of the Dead/Spirits were generic for the entire nWoD. Hunter was the book that actually took mortals, gave them organization and abilities, and set them lose on the world. It was the closest thing to a mortal-specific release after the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, yeah. Mortal 2e did &quot;eat&quot; a lot of Hunter stuff. A lot of people actually called Hunter mortal 2.0 back when it first came out for a reason - it included almost all the stuff you might want for a mortal game. Really, I honestly feel like HtV basically is still just that. Mortal games. It was a focus on mortals that the core book simply didn't get - the original core book was simply too focused on providing generic stuff for all the games instead of a focused mortal. The big thing that Hunter brings is more things that mortals can do. We have example organizations, we have better teamwork rules (tactics), we have better uses for willpower, we have rules for Coding up Morality/Integrity. Those aren't touched on mortal rules, because the mortal rules don't assume supernatural organizations for mortals.<br /> <br /> Because of all the above, I've never really thought of Hunter being a fully separate gameline from mortals. Hunter is mortal taken to the next level. They do all the same things that mortals do. They have the same worries and concerns. Mortals who explore the darkness. The only difference is that hunters have decided to do something about it. Study it, hunt it, socialize it; the different ways the Conspiracies look at supernaturals. (Vision, Zeal and Mercy to use Reckoning terms). I know that a number have classified Hunter as the Power game, and Geist game as the &quot;pick your own stat&quot; game, but for me its always been the opposite. Mortals and hunters are the center of the CofD - they're the (0, 0, 0) starting point for me for touching on the themes and ideas of all other games out there on some supernatural graph. You touch on Mage's study of mysteries, you have your own Hunt, you deal with social situations. There's some Promethean-esk qualities of soul searching and what makes a Monster from a Man, and dealing with the madness of whatever led you to the Vigil. The books of HtV have a heavy focus on other supernaturals rather than their own stuff for a reason. They scaled from street level cells to world spanning conspiracies to adapt to any game you wanted. I know Geist was meant to be the bare-bones, build your own game, but HtV always filled that niche for me better than Geist ever did. </div> </div> </div>At least, all this is my opinion on the matter. I know some of you disagree with my opinion, and feel Hunter is actually a pretty different game. Some others might agree, but have a different way they reached a similar conclusion on the matter. So, here's my question that I would like to put forwards. How do you feel about all this? Are they the same? Different? Should we think of them as different games as Vampire is from Werewolf, and if so, how should it be done? <br /> <br /> Discuss! Lets hear it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T08:55:40-08:00","id":838074,"title":"","content":"I think Mortal and Hunter are different games. Mortals deal with whatever they're facing and then try to go back to their normal lives. Hunters can't turn back. Their former lives are over. The Vigil is their new life.<br /> <br /> To put it as an example: In the Resident Evil series, the classic characters (Jill, Chris, Leon, Claire, Barry) are Hunters (though after RE5, Jill is probably a Deviant instead). The ones that never were seen again (such as the entire cast of the Outbreak games) are Mortals instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T10:24:27-08:00","id":838128,"title":"","content":"For me, the big difference between a blue book game and a Vigil game is that a blue book game has an expiration date. It doesn't necessarily have to be a one-off, but the core story of a base mortal game is regular people being forced to confront the supernatural. After a while, that story has to end. Even if it doesn't have a pre-planned end point and the characters don't all get killed by horrible monsters, at some point they stop being ordinary people. Once the supernatural stops being the thing they all try to avoid and pretend doesn't exist and starts being something they know exists and fight against, it's no longer the same story. It's a story about people who have faced the darkness and made the decision to push back against it. It's a story about Hunters.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, I use mortal for one-off games, or for the starting point of longer running games. I use Hunter as the continuation of that start point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:57:28-08:00","id":838180,"title":"","content":"For me, it's enough that blue book characters often want to just deal with the problem and get back to <i>living</i> in the darkness, while hunters are driven to not just stop with one problem, to seek out other issues and get to <i>doing</i> something about it.<br /> <br /> Purely a mentality thing, but it works for me and my table. It might not work for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:05:19-08:00","id":838212,"title":"","content":"I disagree. For me, a Mortal game is like playing Call of Cthulhu (not exactly, but similar). Mortals are weak, vulnerable, and scared for their lives. While they might do the same thing as Hunters and actively try to destroy supernaturals, that's not the focus. The focus is how the Darkness chips away at their lives, robbing them of their sanity every time they encounter it. Hell, mortals may not even interact with the supernatural directly or even not at all. Here's a bit of an interesting take: perhaps the supernatural doesn't exist. I don't mean that it definitely doesn't, just that its existence is ambiguous. Both the characters and the players aren't quite sure, which can create some real nice dramatic tension, especially for experienced players.<br /> <br /> A good friend of mine who has run tabletops for decades gave me this advice: subvert your players expectations. Do they think the supernatural exists, give them evidence it doesn't. Do they think the supernatural doesn't exist, give them evidence it does. That way, the game is unpredictable to them, you keep them guessing, and you keep the game hella fun.<br /> <br /> With Hunter, you can't do that sort of thing. Hunters hunt after all, so they need something supernatural to deal with. Mortals avoid the supernatural as much as they possibly can, only confronting it when they're cornered. Hunters confront it to begin with. They drive assaults, they build arsenals, they study, they plan. The horror in Hunter is also different. There's a reason only Hunters turn into Slashers when they lose Integrity (or whatever the equivalent is gonna be in 2E). It's not about how the Darkness destroys their lives, it's how the Darkness corrupts them, turning them into one of the monsters they hunt.<br /> <br /> TL;DR Mortals avoid the supernatural AMAP, Hunters confront the supernatural until they die a hero or live long enough to become a villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:25:52-08:00","id":838224,"title":"","content":"Not a bad contrast. Not sure how that disagrees with my notion, but I like it regardless of if it does or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:31:47-08:00","id":838227,"title":"","content":"I've always been fond of the idea that blue book mortals are victims or drawn in by coincidence, while Hunter is about those obsessive people who actually seek the horror out. There's a shift in mentality between a character who is curious about the supernatural in the abstract and one who continues searching for it even after some monster nearly rips his arm off, and the crossing of that line is when a mortal becomes a Hunter.<br /> <br /> Of course, this interpretation works best with the whole &quot;humanity knows the supernatural is out there, but keeps its collective head down and tries to forget&quot; meta-idea; in this context, Hunters are those that cannot keep denying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T17:40:00-08:00","id":838304,"title":"","content":"So, in short, mortal games are either larvae into becoming other things, or put their head back into the sand? I guess my thing is that I've played long term mortal game back in 1e, and it was before Hunter came out. And played a lot like Hunter. So, that's why I think they're the same thing - because that's my experience. So, from the way things sound, any long term mortal game is the same thing as Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T17:47:56-08:00","id":838311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838304#post838304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in short, mortal games are either larvae into becoming other things, or put their head back into the sand? I guess my thing is that I've played long term mortal game back in 1e, and it was before Hunter came out. And played a lot like Hunter. So, that's why I think they're the same thing - because that's my experience. So, from the way things sound, any long term mortal game is the same thing as Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially. It gets weird when you have to wrap your head around &quot;Hunter&quot; not necessarily meaning that you hunt and kill anything; Network Zero are Hunters because they want to document the unknown, Null Mysteriis are Hunters because they want to understand it. Mortals are those who remain ignorant, willfully or not; Hunters are those who can't stay away.<br /> <br /> It's a real shame Mage 2e has capitalized on the whole Obsession thing, because (IMHO) it fits Hunter like a glove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:03:22-08:00","id":838318,"title":"","content":"As a perhaps important note on the subject, it strikes me that that the original Dracula is a Mortal chronicle, and not a Hunter one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-27-2016, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:12:30-08:00","id":838323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838318#post838318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a perhaps important note in the subject, it strikes me that that the original Dracula is a Mortal chronicle, and not a Hunter one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it transitions. When the novel is about Harker's stay in the castle, or Lucy's sleepwalking? That's firmly in mortals territory. But when you have the outlandish expert on the occult and the gun-toting American explorer come in and help your protagonists track Dracula across Europe in order to slay him and his Brides? That goes beyond survival and well into Hunter.<br /> <br /> Then again, I do have the Dracula Dossier's &quot;Harker and friends were secretly competent agents of the British crown tasked with capturing Dracula&quot; interpretation on the brain, so I'm not wholly unbiased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:18:31-08:00","id":838327,"title":"","content":"I can see how it delves into Hunter when they take it upon themselves to pursue Dracula to his motherland and put an end to the threat he is, but here's where I draw the distinction: the cast doesn't venture out to cast a light into the night and be a candle amid the darkness after they've seen the things that may hide within. They deal with the horrors that they stumble into for their own sakes, and remember it in their hearts with fright and inspiration, so they can live their lives safely again.<br /> <br /> And Van Helsing wasn't really much of an occult expert. He had some insight into it because of his general knowledge, but he had to do research, a lot of guesswork, and had no more direct experience than the rest of the group. He did have like six PhDs though.<br /> <br /> That sounds like an amusing turn on it, but I can't recall ever seeing a movie of it, which seems odd!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-27-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:28:52-08:00","id":838333,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that any man who not only knows what plant repels vampires, but has a contact who grows it on speed dial counts as vested enough in the secret world to be a Hunter. But you have a fair point about the group disbanding and returning to moral life after the whole affair is over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:32:17-08:00","id":838337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838304#post838304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in short, mortal games are either larvae into becoming other things, or put their head back into the sand? I guess my thing is that I've played long term mortal game back in 1e, and it was before Hunter came out. And played a lot like Hunter. So, that's why I think they're the same thing - because that's my experience. So, from the way things sound, any long term mortal game is the same thing as Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize I came off harshly with my original one, so I do want to cut it down to the salient point that got buried in some of the negativity.<br /> <br /> Mortals <i>live</i> with the darkness. Head in the sand or eyes wide open.<br /> Hunters <i>do something</i> about the darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:29:54-08:00","id":838373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838337#post838337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize I came off harshly with my original one, so I do want to cut it down to the salient point that got buried in some of the negativity.<br /> <br /> Mortals <i>live</i> with the darkness. Head in the sand or eyes wide open.<br /> Hunters <i>do something</i> about the darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue I see with this, is that while that is the intention the rules don't seem to reflect that. There is nothing stopping the mortal rules from representing tier 1 and tier 2 hunters.<br /> <br /> In Chronicles of Darkness, you can play a guy with Eye for the Supernatural, Esoteric Armoury, Tolerance for Biology, and Occult skill dots.... So a guy who knows about the occult, can identify when something is supernatural, has a stash of gear specifically to fight against the vulnerabilities of various monsters, and has had enough experience that he wont go into shock or get sick from seeing rotting zombies and monsters who have blood spikes coming out of them. In no way does that sorta thing equal &quot;Head in the sand&quot;. Mortals do stuff about the darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:34:02-08:00","id":838380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838373#post838373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue I see with this, is that while that is the intention the rules don't seem to reflect that. There is nothing stopping the mortal rules from representing tier 1 and tier 2 hunters.<br /> <br /> In Chronicles of Darkness, you can play a guy with Eye for the Supernatural, Esoteric Armoury, Tolerance for Biology, and Occult skill dots.... So a guy who knows about the occult, can identify when something is supernatural, has a stash of gear specifically to fight against the vulnerabilities of various monsters, and has had enough experience that he wont go into shock or get sick from seeing rotting zombies and monsters who have blood spikes coming out of them. In no way does that sorta thing equal &amp;quot;Head in the sand&amp;quot;. Mortals do stuff about the darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully there's a new edition coming out that has eight years worth of learning how to remedy that.<br /> <br /> For now, the difference between the two is in tone. It's up to 2e to back it up with mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:40:05-08:00","id":838383,"title":"","content":"I live in a nation that has a hearty population of folks who own a gun &quot;just in case&quot;, but don't actually do anything about crime or terrorism or anything like that.<br /> <br /> Mortals <i>sometimes</i> do something about the darkness. But just because they have an Eye for the Supernatural, Esoteric Armory, Tolerance for Biology(Which could just be a mortician?), and/or Occult(I have dots in Occult and I don't do shit that resembles Hunter life) doesn't mean they make a regular habit of doing things with it. For the most part, they live with it, and they do something as it's needed. A lot of the time, it's &quot;just in case&quot;. It's &quot;So long as they don't bust down my door...&quot; Occasionally, it's pruning.<br /> <br /> There's no <i>sometime</i> with Hunters. There's no &quot;I've got this box of silver bullets <i>just in case</i>&quot; with a hunter. There's &quot;Something has to be done about this&quot; <i>that never leaves the hunter's mind for long</i>. You could never call the extent of what they do pruning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:49:35-08:00","id":838389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838383#post838383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I live in a nation that has a hearty population of folks who own a gun &quot;just in case&quot;, but don't actually do anything about crime or terrorism or anything like that.<br /> <br /> Mortals <i>sometimes</i> do something about the darkness. But just because they have an Eye for the Supernatural, Esoteric Armory, Tolerance for Biology(Which could just be a mortician?), and/or Occult(I have dots in Occult and I don't do shit that resembles Hunter life) doesn't mean they make a regular habit of doing things with it. For the most part, they live with it, and they do something as it's needed. A lot of the time, it's &quot;just in case&quot;. It's &quot;So long as they don't bust down my door...&quot; Occasionally, it's pruning.<br /> <br /> There's no <i>sometime</i> with Hunters. There's no &quot;I've got this box of silver bullets <i>just in case</i>&quot; with a hunter. There's &quot;Something has to be done about this&quot; <i>that never leaves the hunter's mind for long</i>. You could never call the extent of what they do pruning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying All Mortals who have those merits/skills are hunters. I'm saying that you can have hunters with the mortal rules, with no reason to not have them. Simple as that. There is not a single reason you cannot do a hunter with Chronicles of Darkness on it's own. Those thematic reasons your stating, are not rules and are not even suggested in the book. There is no reason why a mortal can't be a hunter without being a Hunter, basically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thankfully there's a new edition coming out that has eight years worth of learning how to remedy that. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm definitely looking forward to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:52:28-08:00","id":838391,"title":"","content":"If you want a mechanical difference, Risking Willpower. Honestly, that's all I need-that expression of the sheer depths of desperation a Hunter can draw from and how far it can take them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:33:24-08:00","id":838417,"title":"","content":"If you wanna talk crunch, yeah, mortals can do most of the things that Hunters can. No argument there. I'll focus on fluff.<br /> <br /> The Vigil turns you into a torch to fight back the darkness, it's true. But it also works like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-kVsxVBz1Mg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the event horizon of a black hole</b></a>. Once the choice is made, all directions only lead further into the dark, even if your fire has long since been snuffed away.<br /> <br /> If you knew for a fact that you were already dead, how would you act on your way out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T21:21:02-08:00","id":838446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838417#post838417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanna talk crunch, yeah, mortals can do most of the things that Hunters can. No argument there. I'll focus on fluff.<br /> <br /> The Vigil turns you into a torch to fight back the darkness, it's true. But it also works like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-kVsxVBz1Mg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the event horizon of a black hole</b></a>. Once the choice is made, all directions only lead further into the dark, even if your fire has long since been snuffed away.<br /> <br /> If you knew for a fact that you were already dead, how would you act on your way out?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be nice if some mechanics backed that black hole up. One reason I added a &quot;power stat&quot; called Initiation as part of my Hunter hacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T21:44:34-08:00","id":838454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Vigil turns you into a torch to fight back the darkness, it's true. But it also works like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-kVsxVBz1Mg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>the event horizon of a black hole</b></a>. Once the choice is made, all directions only lead further into the dark, even if your fire has long since been snuffed away. </div> </div> </div>What fluff-wise prevents this in a mortals game though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:29:48-08:00","id":838475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838446#post838446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd be nice if some mechanics backed that black hole up. One reason I added a &amp;quot;power stat&amp;quot; called Initiation as part of my Hunter hacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838454#post838454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What fluff-wise prevents this in a mortals game though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably the new edition will have an Aspirations equivalent that covers this; giving players the chance to ask themselves &quot;why do you continue your Vigil, despite threats to health and sanity? Why can't you return to a normal life?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:01:27-08:00","id":838485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838180#post838180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, it's enough that blue book characters often want to just deal with the problem and get back to <i>living</i> in the darkness, while hunters are driven to not just stop with one problem, to seek out other issues and get to <i>doing</i> something about it.<br /> <br /> Purely a mentality thing, but it works for me and my table. It might not work for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this post and others say, I very much think of them as two different games, and it's very much a matter of theme and mood. Hunter just has that edge of driven obsession that I don't associate with blue book mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:04:16-08:00","id":838487,"title":"","content":"Same. Like, seriously, Mortals is just dark slice of life, Hunters are this deep dive of fire and shadow. To me, anyways.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is hunters are dwarves.[/sarcasm]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:08:23-08:00","id":838490,"title":"","content":"I think I've just played too much Delta Green to see the fight against the supernatural as anything other than a hideous downward spiral for those involved, doubly so now that the new edition has &quot;your relationships begin to fail because of the stress of your work&quot; as an actual enforced rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T04:26:10-08:00","id":838573,"title":"","content":"Soooooo.... from the sounds of it, it seems that mortal games are basically just people doing everyday things and either willfully being ignorant of the supernatural, or choosing to generally ignore it? Or the mortal PC equivalent of Beast - super crossover madness Sookie Stackhouse style? (Or should we consider Sookie as a high Satiety Beast, which is an entire discussion best suited for the Beast forum?)<br /> <br /> It still sounds like everyone is generally saying that playing Hunter is the only way to have a long term mortal game. Living in ignorance is unsustainable as a long term CofD game, and living with your eyes open means that you are either going to act like Hunter Lite, or get sucked into being a vampire pawn, werewolf pack, etc. At which point, we're no longer dealing with a mortal game, but mortal PCs in a different game.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't buy into that whole &quot;its a matter of degrees&quot; angle that some are suggesting. Because that suggests that you can't be a short term hunter - its a viable plot. Its creating an artificial divide that I don't think that either game supports.<br /> <br /> Can someone make a suggestion for a long term mortal game in the CofD? Because from the sounds of it, I still feel like people are saying that mortal games are unsustainable without becoming a mortal PC in another gameline (or gaining some kind of minor/major template)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-28-2016, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T04:50:27-08:00","id":838576,"title":"","content":"I argue that you can have a long term mortal game, so long as the mortals are being actively harried by the supernatural and don't actually seek it out.<br /> <br /> A group of mortals that is either cursed or simply a natural magnet for supernatural things makes for a fine long-term mortal game. You can also string plots that hinge on the previous one, where the mortals find themselves not being able to put behind the horrible supernatural shit that keeps coming back (for example, the group moves into a haunted house, they resolve the haunting, which leads to a Geist trying to take over the house for its delicious deathly energies, which leads to the Geist's lover, a Vampire, seeking vengeance against the group for killing his lover, which leads to a Horror trying to devour them because the Vampire was keeping it at bay, which leads to a local werewolf feeling threatened by the characters' proficiency at killing the supernatural, and so on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T04:59:10-08:00","id":838579,"title":"","content":"Okay, say I make a character with the Chronicles of Darkness book who is a hunter. What stops that from happening?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:18:41-08:00","id":838586,"title":"","content":"You don't really have the tools to succeed long-term, that's what happens.<br /> <br /> Tier 1 cells eventually either fail or get recruited by a Compact/Conspiracy. Even if you used the Mystery Cult merit to represent that, the benefits can't really hold a candle to Hunter Endowments. Endowments are specifically tailored to fighting the supernatural, sometimes even directly referencing crossover mechanics. Long-term, a purely mortal character that wants to be a Hunter will need Endowments to succeed. Without them, they just can't keep up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:29:02-08:00","id":838590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838579#post838579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, say I make a character with the Chronicles of Darkness book who is a hunter. What stops that from happening?</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that Antagonists established vanilla mortals some kinds of revenge-hunters before HtV came out? Absolutely nothing. The 1e mechanics pushed mortals towards being ghost hunters as well. Ghost stories and Antagonists were two of the first core WoD books to come out, both of which encouraged hunter-like mindsets in mortal games. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:34:05-08:00","id":838593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838586#post838586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't really have the tools to succeed long-term, that's what happens.<br /> <br /> Tier 1 cells eventually either fail or get recruited by a Compact/Conspiracy. Even if you used the Mystery Cult merit to represent that, the benefits can't really hold a candle to Hunter Endowments. Endowments are specifically tailored to fighting the supernatural, sometimes even directly referencing crossover mechanics. Long-term, a purely mortal character that wants to be a Hunter will need Endowments to succeed. Without them, they just can't keep up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually what happens is up to the troupe. The basic Chronicles of Darkness book does provide all of the necessary tools for success. <br /> <br /> Fluff is really not enough to differentiate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:39:41-08:00","id":838594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838593#post838593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually what happens is up to the troupe. The basic Chronicles of Darkness book does provide all of the necessary tools for success.<br /> <br /> Fluff is really not enough to differentiate.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the ST continues throwing challenges that you can easily handle with the non-specific tools you have in the core book, then sure. That's not the logical progression of how hunting goes, though. Otherwise things like compacts, conspiracies and endowments wouldn't need to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:41:46-08:00","id":838595,"title":"","content":"1e Compacts didn't really do anything anyway aside from a support network, which you can do with Chronicles of Darkness mechanics. As for conspiracies, you do not need to be in a conspiracy to be a hunter, I mean two thirds of Hunter are not conspiracies... but even if you did need a supernatural edge, mortals can take supernatural merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:51:32-08:00","id":838597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838586#post838586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't really have the tools to succeed long-term, that's what happens.<br /> <br /> Tier 1 cells eventually either fail or get recruited by a Compact/Conspiracy. Even if you used the Mystery Cult merit to represent that, the benefits can't really hold a candle to Hunter Endowments. Endowments are specifically tailored to fighting the supernatural, sometimes even directly referencing crossover mechanics. Long-term, a purely mortal character that wants to be a Hunter will need Endowments to succeed. Without them, they just can't keep up.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is not quite true. Tier 1 hunter games that don't progress to Compacts or Conspiracy levels exist. No Endowments, no backup beyond your cell. You don't either &quot;fail&quot; or get recruited. Tier 3 hunters are more powerful than mere mortals, yeah. Because they're designed to handle threats on a global scale. Meanwhile, tier 1 games only focus on your local neighborhood, family, and friends. Chances are you won't run into a powerful monster on that scale where you do need more power. Generally speaking, the worst thing you'll run into is a small town cult or a pack/cotorie/etc of other supernaturals. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:52:14-08:00","id":838598,"title":"","content":"It's less about an &quot;edge&quot; and more about having specific tools to fight specific foes. Esoteric Armoury is useful, but it's not the Advanced Armoury Endowment.<br /> <br /> Compacts had Endowments in 1e, btw. They came in the Compacts and Conspiracies book. So that's a full two-thirds of the Hunting community with some specific advantage for fighting the supernatural.<br /> <br /> What blue book mortals lack that Hunters have is <i>specificity</i> in their mechanics and resources. Can mortals make do without? Sure, to a point. There's going to come a point where you will <i>need</i> specific resources or you will fail (assuming your ST follows a gradually ascending difficulty curve). Mortal resources and Hunter resources are different, even after Mortal cannibalised so many of Hunter's mechanics. Hunter is still the sole purveyor of anti-monster-specific resources.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838597#post838597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is not quite true. Tier 1 hunter games that don't progress to Compacts or Conspiracy levels exist. No Endowments, no backup beyond your cell. You don't either &quot;fail&quot; or get recruited. Tier 3 hunters are more powerful than mere mortals, yeah. Because they're designed to handle threats on a global scale. Meanwhile, tier 1 games only focus on your local neighborhood, family, and friends. Chances are you won't run into a powerful monster on that scale where you do need more power. Generally speaking, the worst thing you'll run into is a small town cult or a pack/cotorie/etc of other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have my books on me right now, but I remember a paragraph in one of the books (may have been the core book, even) that spoke about the impermanence of Tier 1 cells. Tier 3 play isn't always some globe-trotting X-COM type of thing, it can easily be a local cell that has Endowments and can call for backup under certain circumstances, but is expected to follow certain rules.<br /> <br /> In fact, this came up in this very forum about how the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy separation didn't always (or even commonly) match up with the three tiers of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 02-28-2016, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:10:49-08:00","id":838605,"title":"","content":"You completely miss the entire point. I was discussing how tier 1 hunter games do exist, do succeed, do survive, and don't have Endowments or Compact / Conspiracy backup. I don't really care about tier 2/3 power differences - that has zero bearing on this discussion. Its a simple fact of the matter that hunters without organizational or specific tools succeed. <br /> <br /> Because here's something you miss - every supernatural comes with built in Banes. Its pretty common knowledge that you use silver against wolves, stakes and sunlight against vampires. Iron and fire are common weapons against a wide variety of supernatural threats in myth and popular culture. And that's enemies with physical bodies. Against ephemeral entities? That's what research rolls are for, and everyone uses the same mortal-based system to discover ephemeral entity weaknesses. Hells, most of the time, most people don't even realize that they need to deal with a disembodied entity - ghosts and spirits need physical anchors in the mortal world. Destroy the physical, you effectively banish the ephemeral. Destroying a cursed totem effectively banishes whatever was empowering said curse. Wood chipper and explosives work here.<br /> <br /> This isn't D&amp;D. An assumption that you &quot;go up in level&quot; and fight monsters of greater difficulty is not a good assumption to have. Nothing is forcing you to progress from apprentice to heroic to paragon and then epic levels of games. Its not even the default assumption of the game. While nothing stops you from playing like that, its not assumed that games will go that way either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:15:13-08:00","id":838607,"title":"","content":"Again, it was specifically written in one of the Hunter books that the Vigil gets progressively harder and Tier 1 Cells don't last for long, directly contradicting everything you said.<br /> <br /> If you can't wait for me to get back home in roughly 12 hours and attempt to find you a quote, I recommend you peruse the books yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:38:45-08:00","id":838616,"title":"","content":"This definitely is a blurry distinction, and something the upcoming second edition of Vigil will have to tackle. I'm not sure if trying to force a separation between core book mortals and tier 1 hunters is a good idea, though. The difference between a mortal character made using the core book and a tier 1 hunter is primarily that of goals and mentality, so Hunter: the Vigil 2e should make it clear and simply present rules and systems that are useful for monster-hunting mortals. The distinction is that of tone and theme, and those can change easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:40:02-08:00","id":838617,"title":"","content":"Very few last for long on the Vigil, be it tier 1, 2 or 3 game. Hunting supernaturals has a high turn over rate, Shadow. You're basically a soldier on the front lines of battle. That's a high mortality rate, no matter the tier, unless you are lucky enough that you survive to retire to a cushy desk job, or something else away from doing the fighting yourself. And, yeah, people having your back is generally accepted to be a good thing. <br /> <br /> And that has absolutely no bearing on this discussion. There are examples of tier 1 Hunter games that do succeed, and aren't crushed like you are suggesting. And that's all that matters - we're looking at things from a meta game perspective on what kinds of stories are possible. Can you run a successful tier 1 HtV game without going up? Absolutely. Does the game force you to grow in tier? Absolutely not. That's the heart of the matter. We're discussing tier 1 games, and their viability. There are examples that succeed. Therefore, its possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:51:44-08:00","id":838619,"title":"","content":"Nobody is saying Cells don't succeed. What is being said is that, long-term, Tier 1 Cells that don't die get noticed by Compacts/Conspiracies and offered a chance to join, particularly aggressive recruiters like the Cheiron Group (the Cheiron write-up in Compacts and Conspiracies actually goes into great detail about how they have an entire branch dedicated to handling cells via liaisons). A good amount of the time, those Tier 1 cells remain Tier 1, even though they're now part of a greater group and have access to endowments.<br /> <br /> If your ST wants to prolong a Cell game while ignoring what the book says normally happens, that's their prerogative, just like with any other homebrew/houserule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:42:11-08:00","id":838713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838579#post838579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, say I make a character with the Chronicles of Darkness book who is a hunter. What stops that from happening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Risking Willpower as a direct manifestation of a of the hunter's deeper desperation and obsession and Hunter Experience as a direct manifestation of that desperation pushing the Hunters to chase and learn greater skills. Neither of those exist in the Chronicles Corebook and are central features of a Hunter, both mechanically and narratively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-28-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:54:04-08:00","id":838717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838573#post838573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooooo.... from the sounds of it, it seems that mortal games are basically just people doing everyday things and either willfully being ignorant of the supernatural, or choosing to generally ignore it? Or the mortal PC equivalent of Beast - super crossover madness Sookie Stackhouse style? (Or should we consider Sookie as a high Satiety Beast, which is an entire discussion best suited for the Beast forum?)<br /> <br /> It still sounds like everyone is generally saying that playing Hunter is the only way to have a long term mortal game. Living in ignorance is unsustainable as a long term CofD game, and living with your eyes open means that you are either going to act like Hunter Lite, or get sucked into being a vampire pawn, werewolf pack, etc. At which point, we're no longer dealing with a mortal game, but mortal PCs in a different game.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't buy into that whole &quot;its a matter of degrees&quot; angle that some are suggesting. Because that suggests that you can't be a short term hunter - its a viable plot. Its creating an artificial divide that I don't think that either game supports.<br /> <br /> Can someone make a suggestion for a long term mortal game in the CofD? Because from the sounds of it, I still feel like people are saying that mortal games are unsustainable without becoming a mortal PC in another gameline (or gaining some kind of minor/major template)?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a certain amount of cynicism going on here.<br /> <br /> Consider that when we say &quot;problem&quot; we're not saying that <i>everything</i> is a problem. It's a mystery, and there should be something horrific to it, but there's room for awe, even wonder. You can go and investigate strange things that only seem like danger.<br /> <br /> Also, consider that a mortals game doesn't need constancy. THere's no sane reason a Hunter game doesn't imply action, even in the downtime, that involves...well, hunting the dark. Mortals can go several months, even years, without actively engaging in the darkness.<br /> <br /> Also consider that some mysteries can be exceptionally long to investigate and handle, that the player characters do balance investigating with their lives.<br /> <br /> Also, just consider the contrast in those two words. Hunters deal with hunts, mortals deal with mysteries. They might consist of the same things, but the attitude is different.<br /> <br /> Living with your eyes open but not chasing the darkness is certainly sustainable-it just means that while you're aware of it, the central feature of your life is not doing something about that. You can do that without chasing down facts persistently about the darkness or becoming prey to someone else. It might not be easy, but no one ever said anything worthwhile is.<br /> <br /> When I suggest slice of life, I'm not joking. Give that a go for a long term game. Or make it a long term mystery that doesn't revolve on the desperation and obsession of hunters.<br /> <br /> Finagle with your preconceptions and consider other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:12:11-08:00","id":838723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838717#post838717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I suggest slice of life, I'm not joking.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. I missed mention of Slice of Life before. That actually makes sense to me - I understand Slice of Life stories better than the rest of the explanations. Okay. Thanks, I think that resolved my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:14:52-08:00","id":838724,"title":"","content":"Yay! I found out how to explain myself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:31:20-08:00","id":838809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838594#post838594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the ST continues throwing challenges that you can easily handle with the non-specific tools you have in the core book, then sure. That's not the logical progression of how hunting goes, though. Otherwise things like compacts, conspiracies and endowments wouldn't need to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't. You can pretty easily build them all using the various &quot;blue books&quot;. The only truly novel mechanic in Hunter is the odd ability to risk Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T14:33:08-08:00","id":838811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838809#post838809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't. You can pretty easily build them all using the various &quot;blue books&quot;. The only truly novel mechanic in Hunter is the odd ability to risk Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue most Endowments, if not all of them, are rather new in terms of giving mortals specific tools and resources to deal with supernatural creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T16:17:34-08:00","id":838845,"title":"","content":"The thing about Endowments is that there's no firm mechanical reason to limit them to Hunters. <br /> <br /> The sky's the limit as far as troupe level innovation goes.<br /> <br /> YMMV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:20:56-08:00","id":840168,"title":"","content":"there is also no mechanical reasons to decide Disciplines must be powered up with Vitae, or that regular people won't be able to activate Contracts using its Catch. The reasons are that Disciplines are designed to represent what a vampire or a changeling can do, and other beings don't. The same is for Endowments- notice I don't say &quot;an Endowment&quot;, but plural. There is nothing wrong in a certain person having a Relic, for example- but having the same access to Relics an AKD hunter has makes no sense. Mechanics are meant to represent the themes of the game, after all- and in the game, they are not meant to be &quot;cool and shiny powers&quot;, but a representation of the conspiracy's resources, knowledge and connections. The fact that something is a merit doesn't mean it does not have prerequisites, and membership in a certain organization is more than an appropriate prerequisite.<br /> <br /> This is a very old argument in the forums, but the point is this- a game is about telling a certain story. Mechanics are meant to bring that story to life. Opening Endowments as whole to anyone harms that story's themes which were established by the developer. No one force you to play it that way- but the game itself has stories it is meant to tell, and it usually draws fans who enjoys those kinds of stories. Such a change feels, to me at least, unnecessary because it both harms those themes and because hacking it into your setting in case you don't like them is not something hard to do- you just need to decide &quot;in my table, everyone can buy Castigations&quot;. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:49:01-08:00","id":840187,"title":"","content":"I agree with LostLight except on one fine detail: I don't agree that Endowments must represent a Conspiracy. I have always been a supporter of opening Endowments to character concepts where it fits, and I would argue that your Tier 1 cell priest being a Hunter with a Benediction Endowment is a lot different than if he's a regular mortal, even if he has one of the core book's Supernatural Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:31:40-08:00","id":840244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=838391#post838391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a mechanical difference, Risking Willpower. Honestly, that's all I need-that expression of the sheer depths of desperation a Hunter can draw from and how far it can take them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't yet read the whole topic, so this may have already been addressed; but to me, the chief mechanical difference between a blue-book mortal and a hunter is Practical Experience \u2014 which can be interpreted as mundanely as \u201cif you're constantly running into the supernatural, you learn quickly or you die\u201d, or more along the lines of \u201cyou know how most people forget the supernatural (and, by implication, forego some of the lessons that might otherwise have been learned)? Hunters don't. Those extra lessons learned because you <i>don't</i> forget? That's Practical Experience.\u201d Either way, hunters are always confronting the supernatural, and they're learning to adapt very quickly \u2014 faster than a blue book mortal would if he was constantly confronted by the supernatural. <br /> <br /> Also: when this came up in a discussion with Monica, someone suggested that a hunter's five questions for Breaking Points should replace \u201cwhat have you forgotten?\u201d with \u201cwhat can't you forget?\u201d implying that regular mortals try to forget about supernatural encounters while hunters tend to be driven by the supernatural encounters they've had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:15:34-08:00","id":840271,"title":"","content":"Risking Willpower was tied to more dramatic scenes in my mind than Practical Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T21:01:03-08:00","id":840372,"title":"","content":"OTOH, Hunter 1e didn't have people earning Beats (regular <i>or</i> Practical) mid-game; so Risking Willpower was uncontested for connection to dramatic scenes. With the advent of ChroD, that's no longer the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T02:43:40-08:00","id":840503,"title":"","content":"Practical Experience? Even if we consider Xp an ooc resource?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-02-2016, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:01:16-08:00","id":840661,"title":"","content":"Yes. The difference between a blue book mortal and a hunter is an OOC one; so it makes perfect sense for the game systems representing that difference to likewise be OOC. <br /> <br /> Besides, Willpower is every bit as much of an OOC resource as Experience is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:11:40-08:00","id":840702,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you're saying that the only difference is from a meta-game level, and not a story one. Do you feel there's not a significant amount of difference between a long term mortal game and a hunter game, if we ignore the mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:08:03-08:00","id":840745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=840168#post840168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very old argument in the forums, but the point is this- a game is about telling a certain story. Mechanics are meant to bring that story to life. Opening Endowments as whole to anyone harms that story's themes which were established by the developer. No one force you to play it that way- but the game itself has stories it is meant to tell, and it usually draws fans who enjoys those kinds of stories. Such a change feels, to me at least, unnecessary because it both harms those themes and because hacking it into your setting in case you don't like them is not something hard to do- you just need to decide &quot;in my table, everyone can buy Castigations&quot;. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A game that only tells a certain story is not also a sandbox game. I don't see anything in your argument that clearly articulates why Hunter couldn't just be a &quot;blue book&quot; supplement the way that Slasher was.<br /> <br /> (Note for the record: I do not support Hunter being a &quot;blue book&quot;. I am playing the Devil's advocate.)<br /> <br /> Regarding disciplines and such I think we agree to disagree. These things are part of templates. Templates are a game mechanic designed to differentiate mortal characters from those who aren't. Mages might by as squishy as mortals but mages aren't mortals. Hunters on the other hand...<br /> <br /> I might also say there's no reason not to upgrade mortals to other templates. In the case of Hunters though, I'd strongly consider just letting them purchase things but, then again, there are reasons I hacked Hunter 1e to have a &quot;power stat&quot;. (I like it when game systems have some consistency throughout but also I don't think of hunters as mortals. Fightning back against the supernatural leaves one changed (or tainted if you prefer).)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 03-02-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:44:50-08:00","id":840766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/838068-hunter-versus-mortal-games-differences?p=840702#post840702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like you're saying that the only difference is from a meta-game level, and not a story one. Do you feel there's not a significant amount of difference between a long term mortal game and a hunter game, if we ignore the mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that someone was asking what the mechanical differences might be; so I focused on mechanical differences, bearing in mind that Hunter 2e is still in the early stages of development. If you want the story differences, I'd say that hunter stories are calibrated for mortals confronting the supernatural, while ChroD mortals stories are calibrated for the supernatural confronting mortals. The former is called <b>Hunter: the <u>Vigil</u></b> for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:06:29-08:00","id":840784,"title":"","content":"Hunter is a different gameline because its genre, theme and mood are different from the theme of the Core book- a mortal game is a game about mysteries and fear, madness and things which lurk in the dark. It is a game about losing control, getting pulled into the darkness and getting out of there scarred and broken- if you get out at all. A mortal deals with things he can't understand, without external support, which draws him more and more into the shadows.<br /> <br /> An Hunter game is about sending light into the shadows- it is about people who use what ever they have, any desperate resource in their hand, jump into the darkness and win. It is a game about mortal men and women who can actually make a difference. You spit in the eyes of the devil and get out alive. You have support in the form of a local cell, of a compact, of a great conspiracy who is able to withstand years and decades and maybe even a millennium or two and surviving the countless assaults made by the monsters in the dark. They are the reason vampires uphold the Masquerade, this is why the Herd Must Not Know. It is about humanity taking a stand- and doing what ever it takes to fight the endless battle against the monsters, even if you need to sacrifice some of your humanity by doing so.<br /> <br /> As for why it should not be a Blue Book- Blue Book supplements are about certain phenomena, something which doesn't really have its own setting, philosophy and influence on the rest of the world in which the Chronicles of Darkness takes place. Inferno? everyone has their own Hell. Innocents? Everyone has children. Slasher and Changing Breeds are a bit different, but the first was originally developed as an Hunter book and it feels that way for many reasons, while that is the CB's least of its worries, especially since many people prefer the WAtP's version. Hunter could be a Blue Book, but that would require you to throw away most of the things above 1st tier and some of the lore of the game, making it into a vary different game. At best you would get something at the style of Hunter's Hunted and Year of the Hunter in WoD, which was kinda all over the place IMO.<br /> <br /> Hunter has its themes, which usually create certain types of stories- it is just as &quot;sandboxy&quot; as Mage or Vampire, in that that Mage eventually leads you into investigating Mysteries while Vampire focus around political struggles and personal horror. Hunter is a game of &quot;sending light into the shadows&quot;- which allows you to tell a wide range of stories, but eventually there is something common in those stories: you are meant to be small and meaningless in front of the darkness, yet you still punch Cthulhu in the face. Why? Because that is what hunters do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:17:59-08:00","id":840829,"title":"","content":"Also, dismissing a game's theme, mood and genre because you can have another game that replicates it is like saying that you can run an all-Thyrsus or all-Gangrel game and replicate a Werewolf game, and therefore dismiss Werewolf's theme, mood and genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:35:06-08:00","id":840888,"title":"","content":"On a concrete level with the exception of will power risking, and certain endowments like those granted to the Lucifuge, mechanically the ChoD corebook ate Hunter. To be fair it ate the God Machine Chronicles as well.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise its too subjective for an absolute answer, what the corebook and hunter means to their fans is personal, so their is no objective truth that can answer this question.<br /> <br /> For me you could run a Hunter style game with the new corebook, doubly so if you add in hurt locker. <br /> <br /> You have horrors, ghosts, spirits, angels, hit men, cultists, the rules for the Claimed and Reverants, and people with freakish supernatural abilities, so you have plenty of monsters to hunt.<br /> <br /> You have MCI, investiagation merits, and Supernatural merits as place holders for Endowments.<br /> <br /> Is a enough to play a hunter style game where you hunter of supernatural mysteries and creatures, yes absolutely.<br /> <br /> Is an a subsititute for Hunter: The Vigil, no because so much of the game is in the organizations, because it lacks the willpower risking mechanic, and much of the fluff.<br /> <br /> Still I've always looked at Hunter as an expansion and focusing of the core mortals setting more then a new splat.<br /> <br /> But again this is all subjective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:40:59-08:00","id":840926,"title":"","content":"Stuff that Hunter 1e (as modified by Mortal Remains) has that ChroD core doesn't:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Risking Willpower<br /> \u2022 Tactics<br /> \u2022 Endowments (including R&amp;D)<br /> \u2022 the Code<br /> \u2022 many Compacts, detailed and ready for use in your Chronicle<br /> \u2022 many Conspiracies, also ready to use. <br /> <br /> That's off the top of my head, and I'm certain there are others I've missed. ChroD hasn't eaten Hunter. It's taken a bite out of it, sure; but just a bite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:45:10-08:00","id":840928,"title":"","content":"BTW, ChroD <i>did</i> eat GMC; it was a light snack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:25:25-08:00","id":840982,"title":"","content":"Then there's stuff that Hunter 2e can <i>add</i>. There's a lot of tonal and atmospheric differences between a corebook mortal game and Hunter that can be reflected mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}